  "rationale": "The throughput constraint (>=250 MSPS, 1 sample/clock) eliminates iterative (N+3 cycles/result) and makes unrolled_k marginal (ceil(N/k)+3 cycles/result; even with k=8, N=12 gives 5 cycles/result, requiring >1250 MHz Fmax which is unrealistic on Artix-7). Pipelined and pipelined_m are the only viable families for throughput. I allocate 50% to pipelined (the primary area/accuracy trade-off family) and 30% to pipelined_m (which can reduce area via fewer registers). 20% goes to unrolled_k to confirm infeasibility. Parameter ranges focus on data_width 14-20 and n_iter 12-18 where accuracy_bits crosses the 13-bit threshold (max_abs_err <= 2^-13 = 0.00012207). angle_guard and frac_guard ranges are kept tight to explore the accuracy/area trade-off efficiently. Rounding is included as a choice since it affects accuracy at no significant area cost."
